#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119653 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "38fce106-2ba8-554c-ace3-a5731d15a635" :question/math-academy-id "e-4949" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation ![](images/f9/f9fe9fa5e18e286ac7e026df2667c7a8ce259cd2c0416efe85d66d2546358dfd.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector ![](images/9e/9e7b8bc888dbf7a764c0d5b9533758277b59e78d476a3cfe7bbfb2fcac7e7363.svg)\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+24-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,6\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119654 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "74693316-2e5a-5821-87a5-fdc5b8719c82" :question/math-academy-id "e-4950" :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,-2,-1)$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle = 4,$ find the shortest distance from $P(0 , -1 , 2)$ to $\\Pi.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-2,-1⟩-⟨0,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+0+6|}{\\sqrt{4+0+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,8\\,|}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119655 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1538dde4-ab62-502e-8efe-7f37628ab861" :question/math-academy-id "e-4951" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3 , -10 , 3)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $2x+y-2z = -1$." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=4$ and $y=-5$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z & =-1 \\\\ 2(4)+(-5)+1 & =2z \\\\ 4 & =2z \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(4, -5, 2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overrightarrow{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-5,2⟩-⟨3,-10,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle a,b,c \\rangle.$ So, for the plane $\\Pi,$ we have $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 1, -2 \\rangle.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+5+2|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,9\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1bcf37-bd86-518e-aede-5addbc97699f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260269} {:answer/id #uuid "59b5fe8c-5178-580c-8f7a-66873832ec9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260642} {:answer/id #uuid "88058d4a-9c93-58e8-8a93-6bee79401fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261061} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a0b17a-e727-58fc-a945-2805ffef7542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261877} {:answer/id #uuid "ff90ee60-4b7a-54cd-af1f-b95d8d140b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff90ee60-4b7a-54cd-af1f-b95d8d140b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262116} :answer-field/id #uuid "84f58d02-2871-5109-a5be-ccd4ac8940b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aec3d295-8d51-5dda-ba42-3f14845dd36d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129095" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(2,-1,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-3)\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-6-4|}{\\sqrt{16+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-22|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85bfeaad-8fb2-554e-8b2b-d6d9ed270b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261036} {:answer/id #uuid "bd225387-6f08-563a-93e5-580bc2de3fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261545} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f76626-293d-5a1e-8f85-4c41b77781d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261718} {:answer/id #uuid "f31c25d9-affe-52b8-9d24-8d18f213abac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261999} {:answer/id #uuid "f77957ce-cde7-579a-b04a-0021d67a5621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0f76626-293d-5a1e-8f85-4c41b77781d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261718} :answer-field/id #uuid "115d5aec-aeb8-5f5b-ae56-1f5bd75035da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "207cee96-48ff-5895-931d-4abf12241582" :question/math-academy-id "q-129096" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,1,4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨3,-2,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,4,-4⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(3,-2,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-2,1⟩-⟨-3,1,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,-4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a92d928e-1d05-5a2c-8a13-b4b2ac358487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261355} {:answer/id #uuid "b65672ab-0c5c-5d72-ac1e-dabd447776a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261476} {:answer/id #uuid "b673a58a-20af-57eb-b855-61aa31129841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261477} {:answer/id #uuid "c8758111-549c-50e6-987d-aa18fe164d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261648} {:answer/id #uuid "ec5a150d-29da-575d-a84b-8bf4069cb081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b673a58a-20af-57eb-b855-61aa31129841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261477} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6fc720-45dd-52de-b923-8c3e0a788e5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "997f5746-6279-5d4c-b439-ed85502108fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-129100" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-3,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨7,-2,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(7,-2,4).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-2,4⟩-⟨8,-3,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,-3,6⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2-3-6|}{\\sqrt{4+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088db5f4-36d3-5c78-98a0-f200bd4afcc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443241} {:answer/id #uuid "168db077-1d3d-5cb0-b6aa-9a45c778361c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443242} {:answer/id #uuid "4a2a87c7-4871-52b2-9751-1dcf545d8473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{11}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443246} {:answer/id #uuid "9c4b18bd-d214-5ab3-980a-bcf8c20a44a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443253} {:answer/id #uuid "a192f294-392f-523d-b854-34cf2ca91ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{11}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "088db5f4-36d3-5c78-98a0-f200bd4afcc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443241} :answer-field/id #uuid "161dc5e7-caef-534f-b118-60aceff59caf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "072e9e45-d148-5a1a-9029-08725d744a80" :question/math-academy-id "q-129126" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,4,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,1⟩=9.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,1⟩ & =9 \\\\ -3x+y+z & =9 \\\\ z & =9+3x-y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=1$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=9+3(1)-(1)=11.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(1,1,11)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,11⟩-⟨-3,4,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-3,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,1⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-3+4|}{\\sqrt{9+1+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-11|}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b8c44f-f4d9-57d8-90d2-99d7decf9188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443244} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1d2c94-d43d-5c24-a663-9d1fbcba711f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443252} {:answer/id #uuid "acf35f72-276b-5ae6-8734-c3d72972ffea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443256} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d5ba1e-9709-5d81-81a8-a2db338b2a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443257} {:answer/id #uuid "e134b035-3648-5a34-a02a-44af5b1b5f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acf35f72-276b-5ae6-8734-c3d72972ffea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443256} :answer-field/id #uuid "3647b522-cc39-5b80-86fd-13996ce4e48f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee5f2c99-4524-5cc2-872a-3bdd6d04d82a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129142" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,2,6)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,4⟩=8.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,4⟩ & =8 \\\\ -2x+4y+4z & =8 \\\\ 4z & =8+2x-4y \\\\ z & =2+\\frac{x}{2}-y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=2$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=2+\\frac{2}{2}-1=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(2,1,2)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,1,2⟩-⟨-3,2,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-1,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|5\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10-4-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-30|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{6} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62c4eecf-296e-5516-b53c-79b78ea2b9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260727} {:answer/id #uuid "db5f3fd7-fa3c-5df3-959c-4c7dfb2a5bea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261814} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d44888-330f-5d97-813d-d06228ec63cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261997} {:answer/id #uuid "f962b70f-c02d-55ba-a6e4-84a85c82d4e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262053} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9efcc2-19b9-54f0-bfe5-a15e71fd1354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f962b70f-c02d-55ba-a6e4-84a85c82d4e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262053} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38b182d-b8bf-588a-b715-8c9ecc4e2585" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "091a2bf6-b258-57c8-a9fa-cfb6d9f29751" :question/math-academy-id "q-129161" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-7,2,3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x+2y-4z=18.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2y-4z & =18 \\\\ 4(2)+2(1)-4z & =18 \\\\ -4z & =8 \\\\ z & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,1,-2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,1,-2⟩-⟨-7,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,-1,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,2,-4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|9\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36-2+20|}{\\sqrt{16+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|54|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{54}{6} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a111ed5-0950-5f80-a305-b88ed9c600f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305240} {:answer/id #uuid "301af7be-9990-5644-a09f-8591c11e190d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305606} {:answer/id #uuid "550ff825-0121-5d42-86fc-26ec2448211d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305974} {:answer/id #uuid "7a035d66-c8ba-598a-9f31-b6f53230f100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306314} {:answer/id #uuid "e6cc836a-38c5-57fa-a930-c8ab2303c2c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a111ed5-0950-5f80-a305-b88ed9c600f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305240} :answer-field/id #uuid "0213e27b-7df0-5cad-a899-3c2f13b651db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1df7d5a8-576c-5e6b-b09e-347611e72e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-33454" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(4,-2,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩=27.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩ & =27 \\\\ -3x+2y+3z & =27 \\\\ 3z & =27+3x-2y \\\\ z & =9+x-\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=6$ and $y=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=9+6-\\frac{2}{3}(3)=13.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(6,3,13)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,3,13⟩-⟨4,-2,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,5,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-3,2,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+10+18|}{\\sqrt{9+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|22|}{\\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c60338e-01a1-5dee-8591-c336fa874093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305574} {:answer/id #uuid "3d434f72-d817-5ecc-ac32-f306d8348871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305740} {:answer/id #uuid "4c63108d-37a0-5e05-9e05-a8c63375f3fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305886} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a55a85-35d3-5215-afa4-5ce34145b01c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306949} {:answer/id #uuid "e089a8c7-c335-5973-89cf-0c76d86099e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c63108d-37a0-5e05-9e05-a8c63375f3fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305886} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc585d07-d772-5e65-84ec-8fbe4a5c3c81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f22d111-9bd0-53c0-9506-a867aa25de4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33466" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3,5,-2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(5,9,0).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+8-8|}{\\sqrt{4+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4|}{\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443266 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d85d58b-d2c6-50e6-b647-b9ac50af4bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443243} {:answer/id #uuid "5ad1e3d5-d1ee-5ca4-bb25-a289369682c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443247} {:answer/id #uuid "66952a23-b25c-549f-a606-5d6dda11f34c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443250} {:answer/id #uuid "75964f2d-1d14-5218-b72a-c985ff68e537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443251} {:answer/id #uuid "a40f70a0-ef1e-59d6-9c75-8bb1b576296f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a40f70a0-ef1e-59d6-9c75-8bb1b576296f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443255} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a75b517-d88b-5fde-8c47-3acf225f13a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "152abe46-196c-57ed-801a-b01b3b6e9019" :question/math-academy-id "q-34033" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,0,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $2x-y+2z=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=3$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y+2z & =-1 \\\\ 2(2)-(3)+2z & =-1 \\\\ 2z & =-2 \\\\ z & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,3,-1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,3,-1⟩-⟨-1,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨2,-1,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6-3-6|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,-3\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443267 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "466771cc-d368-518c-a407-118cef3850d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443245} {:answer/id #uuid "5cbe681d-c67b-512a-b210-fd917c390fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443248} {:answer/id #uuid "63d845d3-365f-535b-afff-d5908b0a7da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443249} {:answer/id #uuid "da38d1c3-4b88-53eb-a80c-704d0e6c3e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443258} {:answer/id #uuid "e59f1960-0256-5298-9dd6-cb0ef30a5ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da38d1c3-4b88-53eb-a80c-704d0e6c3e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443258} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d64e0b6-2371-55aa-b403-0c4879d7c148" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2de4bc9-44ca-5148-a12b-218413513154" :question/math-academy-id "q-34071" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(1,1,-1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨3,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-8,4⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(3,0,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,0,1⟩-⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨1,-8,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-8)+2\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+8+8|}{\\sqrt{1+64+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|18|}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59951a54-81a6-5810-af8e-c4fdad49ec94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365885} {:answer/id #uuid "a90ec159-7db0-5edb-89ff-ff9b5943472c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365886} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5bdcd7-37da-5f22-aead-d95e3ecf08f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{61}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365887} {:answer/id #uuid "c4c49b79-c479-5e32-8877-9be777b5b8ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365888} {:answer/id #uuid "1dacb56b-d8ef-5624-9327-cee1233132b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59951a54-81a6-5810-af8e-c4fdad49ec94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365885} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7ca0aa0-a220-5bdc-b0d2-65b3a735f48d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a0536ad-4890-5a1a-ae11-f816e5c8b4de" :question/math-academy-id "q-34073" :question/problem "Given that $Q(0,5,2)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-6,2,3⟩=16$, find the shortest distance from $P(1,-4,5)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨0,5,2⟩-⟨1,-4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,9,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-6,2,3⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot (-6)+9\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6+18-9|}{\\sqrt{36+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|15|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27496ca3-7fad-5a26-b5da-f602f9ca180b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345703} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6421f7-33b1-5c65-8910-c35b1c7a0bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346173} {:answer/id #uuid "7dfaae5e-dea8-5bfb-9c02-5fac3d7fa85d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{109}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346455} {:answer/id #uuid "91d47231-c5cc-56c3-bf8e-35af3b2e786f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346627} {:answer/id #uuid "aae3eb0c-955f-52e9-abf1-f02ce3d8e415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dfaae5e-dea8-5bfb-9c02-5fac3d7fa85d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{109}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346455} :answer-field/id #uuid "022c53e2-a752-5b98-a9ef-cff9a3af128a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6801290-8008-514c-8914-c43c32373fba" :question/math-academy-id "q-80116" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-6,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-8,6,3⟩=24.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,6,3⟩ & =24 \\\\ -8x+6y+3z & =24 \\\\ 3z & =24+8x-6y \\\\ z & =8+\\frac{8}{3}x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=3$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=8+\\frac{8}{3}(3)-2(1)=14.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(3,1,14)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,1,14⟩-⟨8,-6,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,7,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-8,6,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-5)\\cdot (-8)+7\\cdot 6+9\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|40+42+27|}{\\sqrt{64+36+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|109|}{\\sqrt{109}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{109}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae5898c-91fd-500e-a18d-9a613793916b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345586} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf469ee-bfa5-54ad-9ee7-3e8686851ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345859} {:answer/id #uuid "547fec09-9ac4-53fe-bc5f-235373563b18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346067} {:answer/id #uuid "55089e0f-7f2d-5f0a-af43-9bef0b0757bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346071} {:answer/id #uuid "75641616-9478-59af-a091-d9b5df69b71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55089e0f-7f2d-5f0a-af43-9bef0b0757bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346071} :answer-field/id #uuid "05a0dcf4-c48c-52c6-ad65-ce1c700d5ba5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13132844-a558-54b3-bea9-4e5aeb81c059" :question/math-academy-id "q-80118" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-7,5,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-8y+8z=-36.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-8y+8z & =-36 \\\\ 4(-1)-8(1)+8z & =-36 \\\\ 8z & =-24 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,1,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,1,-3⟩-⟨-7,5,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-4,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-8,8⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-8)+(-5)\\cdot 8|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{8}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|24+32-40|}{\\sqrt{16+64+64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,16\\,|}{\\sqrt{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e17bee3-8a02-51a0-902b-648ddcb92270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345614} {:answer/id #uuid "6464bcc1-d16d-5cb0-a80f-f6367b03555a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346224} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca6c6af-8e29-55f9-9c01-13b97f9802f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346296} {:answer/id #uuid "8110d4bd-ba4c-530a-83b0-df26d06e6b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346479} {:answer/id #uuid "e672771e-7214-548d-ad07-ca6303728298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6464bcc1-d16d-5cb0-a80f-f6367b03555a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346224} :answer-field/id #uuid "71cb2ec2-928a-58ef-9a9b-a21accd24865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ca7603f-8115-5820-93e3-75e60fbf70c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-80119" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(6,6,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-7y-4z=-26.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-7y-4z & =-26 \\\\ 4(1)-7(2)-4z & =-26 \\\\ -4z & =-16 \\\\ z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,2,4)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,2,4⟩-⟨6,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-7,-4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-5)\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-7)+2\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-7)^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-20+28-8|}{\\sqrt{16+49+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,0\\,|}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $P$ lies on the plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "176d1602-8bf5-5374-a9e6-a11eb56ac6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345558} {:answer/id #uuid "83e40ffd-82c5-58c3-8195-51839d2315b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :d